From b786de456f4b7bfbfdb0a6ce67cf8a21065e3a18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:18:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ggml-cuda): one MMVQ launch for the products of one src1

Weights that read the same activation (hyper-connection down and inject,
shared expert gate and up, DeltaNet qkv, gate, beta and alpha, attention
q, k and v) each quantized that activation to q8_1 and ran their own
small launch. At a 4-token verify step that is 665 quantize kernels and
many launches of a few hundred blocks or less.

graph_optimize now moves the MMVQ products of one src1 next to the first
of them (a moved product reads only a weight and that src1, so it can
run there). The evaluator runs up to 4 adjacent ones as one launch on
one quantized src1: each CUDA block finds its matrix and does the same
work as in its own launch, so the results are bit-identical.

Single-column products that an op right after them reads stay in place,
so the bias, scale and GLU fusions keep their adjacent nodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6MCJC4HTKxvuGjKjqDuqQ
